#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203687 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80cffe94-4f90-5bd8-b0b3-c09d54100580" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations"}] :question/id #uuid "058f91e1-7365-5ee5-8c35-0eaa433db282" :question/math-academy-id "e-14616" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A = \\{ -2,0,2 \\}.$\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (-2,-2), (-2,0), (0,0), (2,-2), (2,0) \\big\\}\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the relation is reflexive, irreflexive, or neither." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is\n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x) \\in R$ for all $x \\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x) \\notin R$ for all $x \\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on $\\{ -2,0,2 \\},$ and we have\n\n$$\n(-2,-2) \\in R, \\qquad\n(0,0) \\in  R, \\qquad\n(2,2) \\notin  R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\qquad$ Since $(2,2) \\notin R$ and  $(0,0) \\in R,$ the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203688 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "5a1a0f7a-d39c-5551-a512-5fd1bea5b3cb" :question/math-academy-id "e-14620" :question/problem "![](images/a5/a5d6068e6098da0c8164a2afe50c6b6e184366a1ecec96d4032eb35928b67285.png)\n\nWhich digraphs represent a relation, defined on the set $A = \\{\\spadesuit, \\heartsuit, \\clubsuit\\},$ that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive?" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x) \\in R$ for all $x \\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x) \\notin R$ for all $x \\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nPairs of the form $(x,x)$ correspond to the loops that start and finish at the same node in the directed graphs.\n\nSince $R$ must be neither reflexive nor irreflexive, we require that some nodes (vertices) have a loop and some don't. Among the given options, only digraph III has this property:\n\n![](images/a8/a834e4d6937327c01094409529596d36ac292c590d9ec9defe9d2fbac0bef983.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the nodes $\\spadesuit$ and $\\heartsuit$ have loops, while the node $\\clubsuit$ does not have a loop."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203689 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "76419f6e-45a2-5af2-b048-2f7c323db796" :question/math-academy-id "e-14621" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are reflexive? \n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $2 \\mid (y+x),$ defined on $\\mathbb{Z}$\n\n- $x \\: S \\: y$ if and only if $x  \\not\\mid y ,$ defined on $\\mathbb{Z}$\n\n- $x \\: T \\: y$ if and only if $3 \\mid (x^2+y),$ defined on $\\mathbb{Z}$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x) \\in R$ for all $x \\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x) \\notin R$ for all $x \\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x) \\in R$ for all $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}.$ Notice that \n\n$$\n2\\mid (x+x)\n$$\n\nfor any $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}.$\n\n- Relation $S$ is irreflexive. Indeed, $(x,x) \\notin S$ for all $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx \\mid x\n$$\n\nfor any $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(1,1) \\notin T$ since $3 \\not \\mid (1^2+1),$ while\n\n- $(0,0) \\in T$ since $3 \\mid (0^2+0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80cffe94-4f90-5bd8-b0b3-c09d54100580" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36f3f0bf-a3e9-5aa0-ae1d-c1ea195189e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "for all $x\\in A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416716} {:answer/id #uuid "72067d41-59b5-592f-b53b-26438318bb9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(1,1)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416745} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff805be-2c24-5fe5-bfce-4d7c14cc5dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(2,1)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416752} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e3c218-5ca8-56ad-ae43-4156862f278d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(2,0)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72067d41-59b5-592f-b53b-26438318bb9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(1,1)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416745} :answer-field/id #uuid "68e80583-27f4-549f-817e-8eae51564802" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a759780-1d74-5387-9038-a0d11fb5f254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416693} {:answer/id #uuid "1332b1f3-7971-51f8-884d-3f0bb33c2169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416698} {:answer/id #uuid "1a41c584-e8f5-5ff9-a7e0-804b44214efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "reflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416706} {:answer/id #uuid "3c7861c5-a0c7-5b0c-8e67-6b068c7580a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "both reflexive and irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a759780-1d74-5387-9038-a0d11fb5f254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416693} :answer-field/id #uuid "b41293db-09e7-59d5-a63e-acb26cae819f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6c50a1-6d85-5042-9e1d-f7f320f534bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416720} {:answer/id #uuid "a370b2f4-4dcb-50e9-aa5e-c6d8cb3a8759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,x)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416771} {:answer/id #uuid "b464ada9-c049-50e4-b6c5-7fd6ec4a9d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,x)\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416779} {:answer/id #uuid "f5105ed3-40e2-5038-b1d9-6e95da5b8b23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d6c50a1-6d85-5042-9e1d-f7f320f534bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416720} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd502ea7-b1ea-5eaa-be81-70b834e4b3c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2bcd445f-52b3-5de6-8b46-eb7aa3382e40" :question/math-academy-id "q-212140" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A={0,1,2}.$ \n\n$$\nR={(0,0),(0,1),(1,1),(2,0),(2,1)}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}, \n\nthe relation is \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on ${0,1,2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n(0,0)\\in R,\\,(1,1)\\in R,\\,(2,2)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(2,2)\\notin R$ $\\text{and }(1,1)\\in R,$ the relation is $\\text{neither reflexive nor irreflexive}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ed66ce8-a1ef-5ea8-befa-e99b6d7f0a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/84/847bcee3b9f9fc6672d5858111866141e043e390605cd92fb5579fd5193d7df4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416695} {:answer/id #uuid "52a9053f-f7fe-5c5a-8cb7-8caa90a4b936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/95d0b20c7f11f2242c5e22ed8d66721cd8f0076ea5f0c8f0a996d8536fbd2a35.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416729} {:answer/id #uuid "ab36a133-53cf-525b-b5f5-ae532b953a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dd/ddfa6dfdf196e05ed653672d0e7c4369c75674e885d98b89abf1fdf0e4425474.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416776} {:answer/id #uuid "d540945e-54e2-56f2-a282-982559d38faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cf92336ff9f0a22f7ab5f30e3f3b336dab6f884b72a8deeccfdb00c3f926c5a7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416792} {:answer/id #uuid "e4641094-b746-50c3-b042-2477f64a542e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/90/903c7d67b71386355439cb39a724c6be874ba4c7e3026343d91b429e649fac81.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ed66ce8-a1ef-5ea8-befa-e99b6d7f0a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/84/847bcee3b9f9fc6672d5858111866141e043e390605cd92fb5579fd5193d7df4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416695} :answer-field/id #uuid "62376fe5-0d16-504c-b19e-3a83d24ff291" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d46c6540-3ee2-574b-ab89-04b06559d4b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-212207" :question/problem "Which of the following digraphs represent a relation, defined on the set $A={1,2,3},$ that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive?" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nPairs of the form $(x,x)$ correspond to the loops that start and finish at the same node in the directed graphs.\n\nSince $R$ must be neither reflexive nor irreflexive, we require that some nodes (vertices) have a loop and some don't. Among the given options, only the following digraph has this property:\n\n![](images/84/847bcee3b9f9fc6672d5858111866141e043e390605cd92fb5579fd5193d7df4.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that nodes $1$ and $3$ have loops, while the node $2$ does not have a loop."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14634958-496e-54f5-b885-eeae73164e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,x)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416699} {:answer/id #uuid "495c688c-9c79-5650-becd-e720994fe31f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416725} {:answer/id #uuid "9fea72e1-ea24-5b0c-b646-d5398d396939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416768} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d0153e-a37f-5f88-a02f-701762bb86d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,x)\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "495c688c-9c79-5650-becd-e720994fe31f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416725} :answer-field/id #uuid "37f15f8e-9c05-53c1-b593-9246c68b848e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416819} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9db9a487-357d-5053-b70e-61ed92cb1178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(-1,-1)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416765} {:answer/id #uuid "9e02b9af-6a66-53ce-b5ca-b2973651bd29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(0,0)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416766} {:answer/id #uuid "f9637fc7-5b65-5648-bffc-c57c0e38a6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "for all $x\\in A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e02b9af-6a66-53ce-b5ca-b2973651bd29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(0,0)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416766} :answer-field/id #uuid "47fe7fb7-8e8a-54d9-8d2f-6039eeb4bf9a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "306872e7-1d7b-5d08-a4d5-765ca66562d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416714} {:answer/id #uuid "34f96acd-fc2a-53e4-af03-f1157ecff40d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "reflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416715} {:answer/id #uuid "473beea7-931e-5978-a041-ecf4a6d95c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416722} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ee89c1-f421-512a-b6dd-9a79b8d20f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "both reflexive and irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "473beea7-931e-5978-a041-ecf4a6d95c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416722} :answer-field/id #uuid "a273d003-dffb-5811-a5d8-4b681c5e1492" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a78cb3d5-72f7-5878-912d-51497cf297ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-212208" :question/problem "Let $R$ be a relation defined on the set $Z$ as follows: \n\n$\\,$ $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x-{y}^{2}=0$ \n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}, \n\nthe relation is \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $(-1,-1)\\notin R$ since the pair does not satisfy the underlying condition:\n\n$$\n(-1)-(-1)^{2}=-2\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- $(0,0)\\in R$ since the pair satisfies the underlying condition:\n\n$$\n(0)-(0)^{2}=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(-1,-1)\\notin R$ $\\text{and }(0,0)\\in R,$ the relation is $\\text{neither reflexive nor irreflexive}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc34d62-1b81-5d86-978c-763c5b1036fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(2,2)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416694} {:answer/id #uuid "204ca137-4335-5470-825e-0717b79cf8e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "for all $x\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416709} {:answer/id #uuid "bba561ba-b6af-55b0-ae72-0463a4b72f2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(1,1)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dc34d62-1b81-5d86-978c-763c5b1036fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(2,2)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416694} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e604926-3a36-5408-9f7c-7bb120698a05" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93e18950-29a8-52a9-b857-947d72ceb229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "both reflexive and irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416757} {:answer/id #uuid "a3afeb18-144e-59cc-aabf-0cce033183ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "reflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416772} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5cae6a-e729-53e2-88b5-5a9de238ea8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416789} {:answer/id #uuid "feafc819-cf17-5297-8433-9423e52907b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf5cae6a-e729-53e2-88b5-5a9de238ea8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416789} :answer-field/id #uuid "69fa6a06-e016-5c5c-be5a-48734df01714" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416827} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2129ea14-351e-5487-85a4-c62570378b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,x)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416710} {:answer/id #uuid "78d5ecdf-122b-58eb-ac26-5fed89e25521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416748} {:answer/id #uuid "9f2553b4-156d-5655-8e80-de4eda022fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,1)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416767} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e953b4-d42b-51c2-96f3-22437543b47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,x)\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f2553b4-156d-5655-8e80-de4eda022fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,1)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416767} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb9fad6c-7818-5c2d-a769-230889739a42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c3deb4f-bd86-5557-b5a7-4c0dc0f448ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-213201" :question/problem "Let $R$ be a relation defined on the set $R$ as follows: \n\n$\\,$ $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $y-{x}^{3}\\ne 0$ \n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}, \n\nthe relation is \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $(1,1)\\notin R$ since the pair does not satisfy the underlying condition:\n\n$$\n1-{1}^{3}=0\n$$\n\n- $(2,2)\\in R$ since the pair satisfies the underlying condition:\n\n$$\n2-{2}^{3}=-6\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(1,1)\\notin R$ $\\text{and }(2,2)\\in R,$ the relation is $\\text{neither reflexive nor irreflexive}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19832d4c-4f38-57f7-bb47-2e4d78cada0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(2,2)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416705} {:answer/id #uuid "59eb980b-caf6-54f9-a10c-5793952ad04d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "for all $x\\in Z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416732} {:answer/id #uuid "b8bbc85b-78bb-5ac5-905b-34d5facbf724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and $(5,5)\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59eb980b-caf6-54f9-a10c-5793952ad04d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "for all $x\\in Z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416732} :answer-field/id #uuid "21daace1-64ff-5ce7-897b-c4554c1fd8c6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "104c8b41-ca6e-57c0-8d42-663c4bc18e77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,x)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416697} {:answer/id #uuid "6cac4573-0da4-5a5f-b13e-cacab51aa082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,x)\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416743} {:answer/id #uuid "76db6319-13a0-5813-bfe7-3b42914cb5da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,5)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416747} {:answer/id #uuid "792a0ee2-6925-501e-9e31-987367dde6bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "104c8b41-ca6e-57c0-8d42-663c4bc18e77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,x)\\notin R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416697} :answer-field/id #uuid "953a509c-0254-5c7a-82f3-a3fdb97787bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47a850bc-ccb2-5cfe-9773-c5fe2f42616e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416723} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd4966d-f600-50e1-85d7-6229bee89aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "both reflexive and irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416751} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4da341-9ee6-5cf4-88ac-dd701d3d9a39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "reflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416756} {:answer/id #uuid "95b90f36-d02a-51d7-95b7-b61a1fa42298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95b90f36-d02a-51d7-95b7-b61a1fa42298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416759} :answer-field/id #uuid "9778012a-e1b1-578f-b273-4592e36ba105" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ccf91b35-7753-51f7-9fcf-6efffb54e68e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213202" :question/problem "Let $R$ be a relation defined on the set $Z$ as follows: \n\n$\\,$ $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $2∤(y-x)$ \n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}, \n\nthe relation is \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nThe relation $R$ is irreflexive. Indeed, since $2∣(x-x)$ for all $x\\in Z,$ we have $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(x,x)\\notin R$  $\\text{ for all }x\\in Z,$ the relation is $\\text{irreflexive}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "003f486a-2600-584c-92ff-478adde52a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416691} {:answer/id #uuid "4c56e2bb-43ed-5906-85e4-b291c9d37ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416727} {:answer/id #uuid "9d2585bc-b01e-5f72-8bd0-21e0708314ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416764} {:answer/id #uuid "a753fcea-864c-5d1d-9515-36b40da1b3f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416775} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc8cdb8-d4be-5768-99b5-0263aa670d03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a753fcea-864c-5d1d-9515-36b40da1b3f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416775} :answer-field/id #uuid "50c36a75-cd57-5a00-815a-7d34757ac50b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1a27c07-b36b-5525-ba6b-847b13ebf516" :question/math-academy-id "q-213228" :question/problem "![](images/03/03ddf06402ad38708d232cf28783c817bf881965d54650eb158e7ffca4ea76a2.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent irreflexive relations defined on the set $A={1,2,3}?$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be irreflexive, we require \n\n$$\n(1,1)\\notin R,\\,(2,2)\\notin R,\\,(3,3)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nThese ordered pairs correspond to the diagonal points on the plots, as shown below:\n\n![](images/b6/b63d99459e8271e70ec36fd417d67565f3d5e77316815d49c235468e174aa1e9.png)\n\n \n\nA plot corresponding to an irreflexive relation must not contain diagonal points. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25029d74-6c31-52ad-8e40-faedc9e473db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420400} {:answer/id #uuid "4d14ebfe-075c-5ad1-ac77-3e3c8fa226f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420401} {:answer/id #uuid "618e807a-28cb-599f-9e9f-ea6004064c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420402} {:answer/id #uuid "b23e5cb8-be50-53e9-bf24-a7374c9dcd80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420403} {:answer/id #uuid "f2516513-8240-538a-acb7-6adbea086ea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d14ebfe-075c-5ad1-ac77-3e3c8fa226f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420401} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed0ab4b8-5966-5883-ba7e-805d59df8d8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5414df0-8556-5960-86b0-386e378b451e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213229" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9cddd6584fee52757b1c7a470a6eeffee3678d569e36025ca70c99e5543c71c2.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent a relation, defined on the set $A={\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\delta },$ that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive?" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be neither reflective nor irreflexive, some of the points $(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),$ $(\\beta ,\\beta ),$ and $(\\delta ,\\delta )$ must be in $R,$ and others must not.\n\nThese ordered pairs correspond to the diagonal points on the plots, as shown below:\n\n![](images/7d/7d4257c9e249f9a4c2a53c5566292e21ae6dfa7f0e08e27042548da2d8e7e000.png)\n\n \n\nA plot corresponding to a relation that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive must contain some diagonal points, but not all of them. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a87d5d0-38bc-5381-9d4b-a87753999a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/32a1efbe08709fe0e4ea4c85f062712e9949518564e96d76ab87fd7e6302c15c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416717} {:answer/id #uuid "809c538a-7cf4-56dd-a4a7-a56104f37ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/327aec97acef435e078395ac70e347d53fcaa9adbf7d1ad9c0011dd2d8a4146d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416753} {:answer/id #uuid "8998a9ec-e02c-584a-a952-14c1c4cb33e2" :