l nodes (vertices) have a loop. Among the given options, only the following digraph has this property:\n\n![](images/67/67e71a9121f014683271e905db7278ee6c11eeff31e707e45d70550042e44c2d.png)\n\n \n\nNote that all nodes contain a loop."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4b47a31-7bda-5366-bac4-1d070776e776" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447f87f9-dffa-5f29-8806-d225d659ee36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/03/0347d6a539b6e3288ff0939da134162ed95de9806e587323dda7052ca9496795.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416721} {:answer/id #uuid "622f3578-83a9-50b4-8a37-a22c010e9338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/59aa9eaaa095cbaf2289def489927888b278829c848b80c297203a030dfc4b62.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416739} {:answer/id #uuid "c865c2be-4f2c-573a-8a7d-ef0e3fdb4dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9db95cf46a9112d2f92e7ab9fe336b28d2da9c26971ba14360bdac772b6918e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416788} {:answer/id #uuid "e692f2d1-6ddc-5aa1-9d7c-917bbfff6ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/42/42e97d14f484c8236ff3a25dbed4c37310861dc9435237f8cd1311e4a8715812.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416799} {:answer/id #uuid "ed13d739-9b67-541e-881c-81942c301938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5c/5ce6940ee50ba454d351130eb65669407c81419db3a7b40c191c3100c8ba362e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c865c2be-4f2c-573a-8a7d-ef0e3fdb4dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9db95cf46a9112d2f92e7ab9fe336b28d2da9c26971ba14360bdac772b6918e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416788} :answer-field/id #uuid "910de2ae-fa21-5a92-9bf9-6d0726ae2ecd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c874a7f-ef16-5ee1-ac09-75fb14ed8d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-213234" :question/problem "Which of the following digraphs represent a reflexive relation defined on the set $A={\\pi ,\\omega ,ϕ}?$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nPairs of the form $(x,x)$ correspond to the loops that start and finish at the same node in the directed graphs.\n\nSince $R$ must be reflexive, we require that all nodes (vertices) have a loop. Among the given options, only the following digraph has this property:\n\n![](images/9d/9db95cf46a9112d2f92e7ab9fe336b28d2da9c26971ba14360bdac772b6918e9.png)\n\n \n\nNote that all nodes contain a loop."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "306be17f-f950-57e2-9cb7-2b33c8a4929e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations Over Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21bdce35-1a6d-5b3f-a49e-4f39f1e7cd62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$S$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416711} {:answer/id #uuid "58ae1950-b540-541c-bb35-734835ed6837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ and $T$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416731} {:answer/id #uuid "7c2cab9d-46e7-5fca-9e2e-839c1847e800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416750} {:answer/id #uuid "a67c2cc7-31d2-5884-b5e7-bd42e8198442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$S$ and $T$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416774} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d8d161-c088-50a0-8cdb-b2dfab2b3cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$S$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21bdce35-1a6d-5b3f-a49e-4f39f1e7cd62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$S$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416711} :answer-field/id #uuid "a904c1ac-f48c-541f-87b2-64440b6f4699" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7095468b-6aec-5ce6-83d1-ea12403a6b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-213240" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are reflexive? \n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x+y)∣10,$ defined on $Z$\n\n- $x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $4∣({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- $x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $x∣(y+1),$ defined on $Z$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin R$ since $2+2=4$ and $4∤10,$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in R$ since $1+1=2$ and $2∣10.$\n\n- Relation $S$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\in S$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\n4∣({x}^{2}-{x}^{2})\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin T$ since $2∤(2+1),$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in T$ since $1∣(1+1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80cffe94-4f90-5bd8-b0b3-c09d54100580" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irreflexive Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c50f2cd-a725-5ab2-b922-726ece1440dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c50f2cd-a725-5ab2-b922-726ece1440dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416736} :answer-field/id #uuid "e314e494-3748-53a1-9f9a-a3e8ff76eb22" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab826688-22e9-5d03-a5c9-fac0134cda3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab826688-22e9-5d03-a5c9-fac0134cda3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416777} :answer-field/id #uuid "e331289f-d2a2-53a6-8619-e9f3015f3a01" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbdfeb37-93cd-58bf-9034-4c86ec249462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbdfeb37-93cd-58bf-9034-4c86ec249462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416796} :answer-field/id #uuid "f355ce46-5c54-5aea-bacc-4b13f9e0cb5f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08d898ff-f576-5e6a-bdf8-9d2e027a5e42" :question/math-academy-id "q-213244" :question/problem "Consider a relation $R$ that is defined on the set $A={\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\gamma }.$ Given that $R$ is reflexive, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix.\n\n|  | $\\alpha $ | $\\beta $ | $\\gamma $ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\alpha $ | {{field-1}} | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $\\beta $ | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |\n| $\\gamma $ | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be reflexive, we require \n\n$$\n(\\alpha ,\\alpha )\\in R,\\,(\\beta ,\\beta )\\in R,\\,(\\gamma ,\\gamma )\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis means that the diagonal elements of the adjacency matrix must all be $1,$  as shown below:\n\n|  | $\\alpha $ | $\\beta $ | $\\gamma $ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\alpha $ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $\\beta $ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $\\gamma $ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80cffe94-4f90-5bd8-b0b3-c09d54100580" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Reflexive and Irre